    {
      "section_id": "SEC054",
      "title": "Training the Wandering Mind",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "If you are going to meditate, you must deal honestly with the fact that your mind will wander unless it is trained. Are you telling me that it will simply sit still on its own? It will not. You must arrest it, put it in a compartment, and say to it, 'I am talking to God now.' This discipline does not come automatically.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA239",
            "SRC006489",
            "SRC006493",
            "SRC006520",
            "SRC006532",
            "SRC006534",
            "SRC006536",
            "SRC006538"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC006489",
            "SRC006493",
            "SRC006520",
            "SRC006532",
            "SRC006534",
            "SRC006536",
            "SRC006538"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA239"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000020",
          "provider_handle": "p20"
        },
        {
          "text": "Train yourself in this way before sleep, and you will never have bad dreams again in the same way. More than that, you can learn to bring a dream back when it carries meaning worth recovering.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA240",
            "SRC006566",
            "SRC006568",
            "SRC006571"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC006566",
            "SRC006568",
            "SRC006571"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA240"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000021",
          "provider_handle": "p21"
        },
        {
          "text": "Samson's father, Manoa, gives us a picture of this. An angel suddenly appeared to his wife, but when she was afraid to speak, the angel went away. Manoa then prayed and asked that the man of God be sent back to them, and the angel returned. What this shows is that a divine encounter, once withdrawn, can be recalled through prayer — just as you can call a dream back.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA240",
            "EX038",
            "SRC006580",
            "SRC006586",
            "SRC006595",
            "SRC006598",
            "SRC006611",
            "SRC006617"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC006580",
            "SRC006586",
            "SRC006595",
            "SRC006598",
            "SRC006611",
            "SRC006617",
            "SRC006566",
            "SRC006568",
            "SRC006571"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA240"
          ],
          "example_refs": [
            "EX038"
          ],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000022",
          "provider_handle": "p22"
        },
        {
          "text": "When you are finished thinking about someone else's problem, ask yourself honestly whether your excessive worry has helped them at all. Often it has not — you have only added yourself into the problem. Your mother may be sick, but your anxious worry about it adds nothing to her healing and only increases your own burden.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA241",
            "SRC006630",
            "SRC006632",
            "SRC006635",
            "SRC006636"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC006630",
            "SRC006632",
            "SRC006635",
            "SRC006636"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA241"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000023",
          "provider_handle": "p23"
        },
        {
          "text": "Let us instead practice life the way a child does. A child's growth in any skill starts small; she must learn life step by step, and she must practice it. In the same way, spiritual life must be practiced gradually, growing from small beginnings.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA242",
            "SRC006641",
            "SRC006649",
            "SRC006652",
            "SRC006668",
            "SRC006677"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC006641",
            "SRC006649",
            "SRC006652",
            "SRC006668",
            "SRC006677"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA242"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000024",
          "provider_handle": "p24"
        },
        {
          "text": "Consider the difference between walking on dry land and being underwater. If you breathe the way you do on land while you are underwater, you suffocate; you have entered another dimension, and you must adapt consciously and correctly to it. Spiritual life works the same way — each dimension of truth requires its own proper adaptation, not the habits suited to another.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA245",
            "EX040",
            "SRC006845",
            "SRC006852",
            "SRC006862",
            "SRC006869",
            "SRC006883"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC006845",
            "SRC006852",
            "SRC006862",
            "SRC006869",
            "SRC006883"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA245"
          ],
          "example_refs": [
            "EX040"
          ],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000025",
          "provider_handle": "p25"
        }
      ],
